==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Aku Gory]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[I.M. Phace]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 4~10 seconds<sup>120f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main danger in this stage lies in the Aku Gory spam that occurs after the base is hit. At this point of the game, I.M. Phace should not be a major problem but still stands as a powerful support midranger. You should bring a few units that counter him such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to make cleanup faster since he's the only other enemy here. There is only one Aku Gory that spawns pre-base hit, so if you find that money is tight or if you use a lot of expensive ubers, it is recommended that you try to stall the first Aku Gory to get as much cash as possible.

Once the base takes damage, lure a bit and burst down as many Aku Gories as you can with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Due to the low magnification on the Aku Gories, a level 30 Awakened Bahamut Cat does exactly enough damage to one shot Aku Gory, however, make sure that your seal is at least level 30 before doing this. After you survive the first 10 Aku Gories, try to kill I.M Phace before more Aku Gories spawn, although they should be easy to deal with unless they stack while your defenses are down.

